<%# The two-column shape shared by every reference page in this demo: a
    sidebar flush to the window's left edge, a content column beside it, and
    the footer inside that column rather than full width below it like every
    other page's (Tailwind's own docs are the model). First built for the
    gallery alone; the documentation pages use the same partial now rather
    than a lookalike of their own, so there is one shell rather than two. %>
<%# The layout renders the site footer for every page that does not carry its
    own. Declared here rather than guessed from a controller name out there,
    which is how /vitral got two: it is pages#vitral, in the same controller
    as two pages that are not shell pages, so no list of controller names
    could have been right. %>
<% content_for :footer_in_shell, true %>

<div class="shell">
  <%= render "shared/shell_nav" %>

  <div class="shell-main">
    <div class="shell-content">
      <%= yield %>
    </div>

    <%= render "shared/footer" %>
  </div>
</div>
